  {
    "id": "traefik-11622",
    "repo": "traefik/traefik",
    "issue_number": 11622,
    "issue_url": "https://github.com/traefik/traefik/issues/11622",
    "title": "Health checking not correctly routing traffic away from unhealthy endpoints - Kubernetescrd",
    "comments": 15,
    "priority_rank": 5,
    "severity": "critical",
    "status": "pr_opened",
    "pr_url": "https://github.com/traefik/traefik/pull/14261",
    "notes": "Root cause: kubernetescrd never set WeightedRoundRobin.HealthCheck on the parent WRR built from multiple IngressRoute services/Weighted TraefikService, so child health-check transitions on ExternalName services never propagated to the parent balancer used for routing. Fix enables propagation only when every child is a plain K8s Service with its own healthCheck (the one case guaranteed safe). Tests added, adversarial review passed, PR opened against v3.7 maintenance branch from rnikhori/traefik.",
    "attempted_at": "2026-11-10"
  },
  {
    "id": "grafana-103076",
    "repo": "grafana/grafana",
    "issue_number": 103076,
    "issue_url": "https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/103076",
    "title": "Grafana/Migrations: Unable to create unique index UQE_alert_rule_version_rule_guid_version",
    "comments": 25,
    "priority_rank": 6,
    "severity": "critical",
    "status": "pr_opened",
    "pr_url": "https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/137398",
    "notes": "Root cause: setRuleGuidMigration never assigns rule_guid to orphaned alert_rule_version rows (left behind after rule deletion), leaving them empty-string and colliding on the later unique index. Fix assigns one synthetic GUID per (rule_org_id, rule_uid) group - no data deleted; a per-row-GUID first draft was caught and corrected by adversarial review. 4 new tests pass. CAVEAT: grafana/grafana now requires signed commits (CONTRIBUTING.md, eff. June 2026); this environment had no signing key configured, so the pushed commit is unsigned - likely needs re-signing before merge.",
    "attempted_at": "2026-11-10"
  },
